I've made some progress with SBLive.  I've now listened through analog in.  It
sounds great.  I was using a very low noise source,  DAT Master tapes I 
mastered.  I noticed some slight noise on the right channel with the faders
cranked between the tracks.  You wouldn't dare leave them at that level for the
program material.   With the faders down the program was close 100db spl
at my ears and there was no noise between tracks.

I tried a midi file with the midi player that comes with KDE.  I don't think I
was getting midi signal out the cable however I heard music from the 
internal synth.   Midi will take a little more time to figure out because 
of all the possible settings. 

